lan: Inspect the board structure using segmentation, then probe with basic actions to understand what's controllable and what the goal is.\n- Revise any item above immediately if `current_frame` or `history` contradicts it.\nend of world model. \nFocus on what changed most recently in `history`, update the target environment change if needed, and separate gameplay-object changes from HUD-only changes.\nWhen ready, call `action(actions)` from inside the `python` tool with the best valid action or ordered batch selected by your code. If your code has found a reliable short sequence, prefer batching it in one call.\nYou may call `action(actions)` more than once in one Python snippet if your search or control loop needs it.\nIf you include assistant text before a tool call, keep it short and use it to update the world model. Helpful optional prefixes are `World model:`, `Goal model:`, `Action model:`, `Recent findings:`, `Open questions:`, `Plan:`, and `Cross-level notes:`.\nWhen calling `python`, emit exactly the tool-call format shown elsewhere in this prompt for this model. Use only that format; do not add markdown fences, prose wrappers, or alternate tool-call syntax. Do not quote or place tool-call markup inside explanatory text; when you decide to call the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 1: you have used 3 of about 39 target actions so far.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "Key findings:\n- LEFT moves the blue bar left by 4 columns\n- RIGHT moves the blue bar right by 4 columns (back to original position)\n- SPACE does NOT move the blue bar, but the green bar still shrinks (from 60 to 58)\n- The green bar at top is a timer/progress bar that shrinks by 2 pixels per action\n- The blue bar is the controllable object\n- The yellow blocks at bottom are platforms\n- The charcoal+magenta blocks at top-right might be a target\nThe goal is likely to move the blue bar to align with something. Let me think about what:\n- The charcoal block is at cols 36-39, rows 1-3\n- The magenta block is at cols 36-39, rows 4-7\n- The blue bar is 4x20, currently at cols 12-31, rows 16-19\nMaybe I need to move the blue bar so it's underneath the charcoal/magenta blocks? That would be cols 36-39. The blue bar is 20 cols wide, so if its right edge needs to be at col 39, its left edge would be at col 20. Currently it's at 12-31.\nWait, let me reconsider. The blue bar needs to be at cols 20-39 to be under the charcoal/magenta (cols 36-39). That would mean moving right by 8 columns from current position (12-31 \u2192 20-39).\nBut wait, each RIGHT moves it by 4 columns. So 2 RIGHT actions would move it from 12-31 to 20-39.\nActually, let me reconsider the goal. Maybe the blue bar needs to drop down and land on the yellow platforms? Let me try DOWN to see what happens.\nActually, the green bar is shrinking - it's a timer. I need to be efficient. Let me try DOWN to see if the blue bar can fall.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# The green bar shrinks by 2px per action - it's a timer\n# Blue bar moves left/right by 4 cols per action\n# Let me try DOWN to see if the blue bar can fall\nresult = action(['DOWN'])\nprint(f\"After DOWN:\")\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nfor n in seg['nodes']:\n    b = n['boundary']\n    rows = [p[0] for p in b]\n    cols = [p[1] for p in b]\n    rmin, rmax = min(rows), max(rows)\n    cmin, cmax = min(cols), max(cols)\n    if n['color'] in ('b', 'N', 'M', 'c'):\n        print(f\"  {n['color']}: [{rmin},{cmin}]-[{rmax},{cmax}] {n['pixels']}px\")\nprint(f\"Result: {last_action_result.get('gameplay_changed')}, {last_action_result.get('no_impact')}\")\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "After DOWN:\n  N: [0,0]-[0,54] 55px\n  c: [1,36]-[3,39] 12px\n  M: [4,36]-[7,39] 16px\n  b: [20,12]-[23,31] 80px\nResult: True, False", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}], "hasExactModelContext": false, "requestIndexWithinTurn": null, "messageCount": 0}}}